  "chapter": {
    "label": "Screens",
    "heading": "Every screen in the file, flow by flow.",
    "body": [
      "The App page in Figma holds 138 phone frames across eleven sections. Twelve are exact copies — the venue flow reuses the whole meetup wizard, and one edit screen appears twice — so 126 screens remain. All of them are below, in the order a person meets them: getting in, finding a meetup, joining or hosting one, talking about it, and the profile that holds the rest.",
      "Ten frames needed care to be shown at all. Six sit at 10% opacity in the file and four under a canvas overlay, so each was rendered on its own at full strength. The sample account's email is pixelated and its profile photo blurred; the venue screens still carry a real coffee chain's brand as a placeholder."
    ],
    "figureCaption": "All 126 screens of the VIN app, in ten flows. Open one to see the whole screen."
  },
